//! # Ordering
//!
//! `ToolCallDelta` is emitted while the model stream drains; the matching
//! `ToolCallItem` only afterwards. `TOOL_CALL_START` is therefore derived from the
//! deltas for a call id, and never from `ToolCallItem`, which would put START after
//! the ARGS frames it must precede. Core gives `name: Some` exactly once per call,
//! but not always on the first delta (`paigasus-helikon-core/src/model.rs`), and the
//! name is the START payload. So the mapper buffers the deltas of a call until one
//! of them carries the name; then START opens the span and the buffered args follow.
